# Line endings are normalised to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Git already stores LF. Without this file, core.autocrlf=true converts to
# CRLF on checkout on Windows, and Prettier — whose endOfLine default is "lf"
# — then reports every file in the repository as misformatted. Validation row
# 1.7 of every phase asserts `npx prettier --check .` exits 0, and on a cold
# clone it did not: 69 files, none of them edited by anybody.
#
# text=auto still lets Git detect and leave binary files alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
